{"id":"4b54ab2a-e433-49eb-b420-4380dea52374","object":"chat.completion","created":1785028101,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required top-level fields\\n    required_fields = ['initial_state', 'max_steps', 'tool_observations', 'transitions']\\n    for field in required_fields:\\n        if field not in case:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Missing required field: {field}')\\n    initial_state = case['initial_state']\\n    max_steps = case['max_steps']\\n    tool_obs = case['tool_observations']\\n    transitions = case['transitions']\\n\\n    # Validate types\\n    if not isinstance(initial_state, str):\\n        raise ValueError('initial_state must be a string')\\n    if not isinstance(max_steps, int) or max_steps < 0:\\n        raise ValueError('max_steps must be a non-negative integer')\\n    if not isinstance(tool_obs, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('tool_observations must be a dict')\\n    for k, v in tool_obs.items():\\n        if not isinstance(k, str) or not isinstance(v, str):\\n            raise ValueError('tool_observations keys and values must be strings')\\n    if not isinstance(transitions, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('transitions must be a dict')\\n\\n    # Validate all states referenced in transitions exist\\n    for state_name, trans in transitions.items():\\n        if not isinstance(state_name, str):\\n            raise ValueError('state names must be strings')\\n        if not isinstance(trans, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(f'transition for state {state_name} must be a dict')\\n        if 'kind' not in trans:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Missing \\\"kind\\\" in transition for {state_name}')\\n        kind = trans['kind']\\n        if kind not in ('action', 'final'):\\n            raise ValueError(f'Invalid kind \\\"{kind}\\\" in state {state_name}')\\n        if kind == 'final':\\n            if 'value' not in trans or not isinstance(trans['value'], str):\\n                raise ValueError(f'Final state {state_name} must have string \\\"value\\\"')\\n        elif kind == 'action':\\n            for sub in ['action', 'next_by_observation', 'default_next']:\\n                if sub not in trans:\\n                    raise ValueError(f'Action state {state_name} missing \\\"{sub}\\\"')\\n            if not isinstance(trans['action'], str):\\n                raise ValueError(f'Action in state {state_name} must be a string')\\n            if not isinstance(trans['next_by_observation'], dict):\\n                raise ValueError(f'next_by_observation in {state_name} must be a dict')\\n            for obs, ns in trans['next_by_observation'].items():\\n                if not isinstance(obs, str) or not isinstance(ns, str):\\n                    raise ValueError('next_by_observation keys and values must be strings')\\n                if ns not in transitions:\\n                    raise ValueError(f'State \\\"{ns}\\\" referenced in \\\"{state_name}\\\" not in transitions')\\n            if not isinstance(trans['default_next'], str):\\n                raise ValueError(f'default_next in {state_name} must be a string')\\n            if trans['default_next'] not in transitions:\\n                raise ValueError(f'default_next state \\\"{trans[\\\"default_next\\\"]}\\\" not in transitions')\\n\\n    # Validate initial state exists\\n    if initial_state not in transitions:\\n        raise ValueError(f'initial_state \\\"{initial_state}\\\" not found in transitions')\\n\\n    state = initial_state\\n    step = 0\\n    trace = []\\n    final_value = None\\n    status = 'max_steps'  # default if loop ends without final\\n\\n    while step < max_steps:\\n        trans = transitions[state]\\n        if trans['kind'] == 'final':\\n            final_value = trans['value']\\n            status = 'completed'\\n            break\\n        # action state\\n        action_name = trans['action']\\n        # Determine observation\\n        if action_name in tool_obs:\\n            observation = tool_obs[action_name]\\n        else:\\n            observation = 'invalid'\\n        # Determine next state\\n        next_state = trans['next_by_observation'].get(observation, trans['default_next'])\\n        # Append trace entry (state before action)\\n        trace.append({\\n            'step': step,\\n            'action': action_name,\\n            'observation': observation,\\n            'state': state\\n        })\\n        # Move to next state\\n        state = next_state\\n        step += 1\\n        # Check if new state is final (to handle immediate final after action)\\n        if state in transitions and transitions[state]['kind'] == 'final':\\n            final_value = transitions[state]['value']\\n            status = 'completed'\\n            break\\n\\n    # If loop ended naturally (step == max_steps) without final\\n    if step == max_steps and status != 'completed':\\n        # Check if current state is final? Actually we would have broken if final was reached.\\n        # At this point state might still be action, but no more steps allowed.\\n        final_value = None\\n        status = 'max_steps'\\n    # If we broke because initial state was final, trace is empty.\\n    return {\\n        'final': final_value,\\n        'status': status,\\n        'trace': trace\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write the solve(case) function for AGENT-RA-02. The case payload contains: initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations (dict mapping tool name to observation string), transitions (dict mapping state to transition definition). Each transition has \"kind\": either \"action\" or \"final\". If \"action\", it has \"action\" (tool name), \"next_by_observation\" (dict mapping observation to next state), and \"default_next\" (fallback). If \"final\", it has \"value\" (string). Also, there might be unknown tools: if a tool is not in tool_observations, then the observation for that tool is \"invalid\" (or maybe we need to define? The candidate artifact says \"invalid-action feedback\". So we need to handle case where action tool is not in tool_observations: observation should be \"invalid\" (or maybe some default? The spec says \"distinguish missing tools and states\". Also for states: if a transition leads to a state not defined in transitions, that might be an error? But we can handle by checking if state exists. Also steps: we start at initial_state, step count. At each step, if current state is final, we stop and return final value, status \"completed\" (or \"success\"? The output schema: status is string, final is null or string. Probably status indicates if we completed or exceeded max steps? Let's think: The output should have status, final, trace. The trace contains steps: action, observation, state, step. The \"final\" is the final value (if reached a final state) else null? And status maybe \"completed\" or \"max_steps\"? The candidate artifact says \"Stop on completion or max steps and return status, final value, and trace.\" So status could be \"completed\" if we reached final state, \"max_steps\" if we ran out of steps without reaching final? Or \"error\"? But the schema only requires a string. We'll define status as \"completed\" when final state reached, \"max_steps\" when max steps exhausted without final, and \"invalid\" if something else? But we must raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. So we need to validate: initial_state must be in transitions, max_steps >= 0, tool_observations may be empty but action tools should be present? For missing tool, observation is \"invalid\"? The candidate artifact says \"invalid-action feedback\" so we should treat missing tool as observation \"invalid\". But what about observation not in next_by_observation? Then use default_next. Also if default_next leads to missing state? That could be problematic but we can treat as error? Probably we should raise ValueError if a transition points to missing state. But the spec says \"raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case\" so we should validate that all referenced states exist. Also ensure transitions dict contains all states. Also ensure kind is either \"action\" or \"final\". Also ensure action state has action string, next_by_observation dict, default_next string. For final state, value string.\n\nWe'll implement solve(case) that:\n\n1. Validate payload: extract initial_state, max_steps, tool_observations, transitions. Check they exist and are properly typed. Raise ValueError if missing or type wrong.\n2. Validate all states in transitions exist, and for each action state, its next_by_observation and default_next exist and are in transitions. Also ensure tool_observations keys? Not necessarily all tools used must be in tool_observations; if a tool is not in tool_observations, we'll treat observation as \"invalid\". But we need to define the observation for missing tool: \"invalid\". That seems appropriate.\n3. Initialize state = initial_state, step = 0, trace = [].\n4. While step < max_steps:\n   - Get transition for current state. If not found -> ValueError.\n   - If kind == \"final\": \n        - final = transition['value']\n        - status = \"completed\"\n        - Append a trace entry? Possibly for final state we might not have action/observation. The schema requires trace entries with step, action, observation, state. For final state, we could record a final step? The candidate artifact says \"A final state terminates without a tool call.\" So we don't add a trace entry for the final state? But the trace may include the step that led to final? Actually the trace is for actions taken. So we only record entries when we take an action. At the start, we are at initial state; if initial state is final, we have no action. Should we record a trace entry? Probably not, because no action taken. But the schema expects trace array; it can be empty. So we can break immediately with final=value, status=\"completed\", trace=[]? But the step counter hasn't started. It's fine.\n   - Else if kind == \"action\":\n        - action_name = transition['action']\n        - Determine observation: if action_name in tool_observations, observation = tool_observations[action_name]; else observation = \"invalid\".\n        - Determine next_state: if observation in transition['next_by_observation']: next_state = transition['next_by_observation'][observation]; else next_state = transition['default_next'].\n        - Append to trace: { \"step\": step, \"action\": action_name, \"observation\": observation, \"state\": current_state } (state before action? Or after? The schema says state field in trace. Typically trace records state before action. Let's define as the state at the beginning of the step. The candidate artifact says \"record the exact observation\" and trace should include state. We'll set state to the state before the action.\n        - Update state = next_state.\n        - step += 1.\n   - Else -> ValueError.\n   - If after update state is final? Actually we need to check again at next loop iteration. But we can also check after updating state; if state is final, we can break and record final? But we haven't used a step for that final state. The trace already recorded the action that led to final. At the moment we update state to final, we break and return final. So we should check if the new state is final. But careful: if we break after detecting final, we should not increment step further. The loop condition will check step < max_steps before next iteration. So we can break after updating state if kind final? Actually we are in an action step; after updating state, if the new state is final, we should treat that as termination. So we can check: if new_state is final in transitions, then set final = transitions[new_state]['value'], status = \"completed\", and break. But we already recorded the action trace. That's fine.\n   - Else continue.\n\n5. If loop exits without reaching final (step == max_steps): status = \"max_steps\", final = null, trace as recorded.\n\n6. Return { \"final\": final, \"status\": status, \"trace\": trace }\n\nMake sure to validate carefully. Also note max_steps includes steps taken? The loop counts each action step. So if max_steps=0 and initial state is final, we can return final immediately. If max_steps=0 and initial state is action, we cannot take any action, so status \"max_steps\" with final null and trace empty.\n\nAlso handle case where initial_state is not in transitions -> ValueError.\n\nWe'll implement as Python function.\n\nNow produce the JSON output with key \"implementation\" and value a JSON-escaped string of the Python source.\n\nWe need to ensure we don't use any non-standard libraries, only standard lib. We'll use json for returning? The function must return a JSON-serializable object (dict). We'll just return dict. No need to import json.\n\nLet's write code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1694,"completion_tokens":2877,"total_tokens":4571,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1664},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1646},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1664,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":30},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}